---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../data/site';

const updated = '2026-03-15';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Accessibility Statement"
  description={`Accessibility commitment and WCAG-oriented features for ${siteConfig.name}.`}
  showSearch={false}
>
  <article class="container-arcade prose-arcade legal-doc w-full max-w-4xl py-8 sm:py-10">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-white">Accessibility Statement</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-arcade-muted">
      Last updated: <time datetime={updated}>{updated}</time>
    </p>

    <p class="mt-4">
      {siteConfig.legalName} is committed to making {siteConfig.name} usable by as many people as possible,
      including people who use keyboards, screen readers, zoom, and reduced-motion settings. We aim to conform to
      the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 Level AA where practical for a static game-discovery site.
    </p>

    <h2>Measures we take</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Skip link to main content</li>
      <li>Semantic headings and labeled form controls on legal pages</li>
      <li>Visible focus styles for interactive controls</li>
      <li>ARIA labels on primary navigation, category filters, and dialogs</li>
      <li>Keyboard support for opening/closing the category menu (Escape closes the mobile drawer)</li>
      <li>Live region announcements when search/category filters change results</li>
      <li>Respect for <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code></li>
      <li>Text alternatives for meaningful images; decorative images marked appropriately</li>
      <li>Language of page set to English (<code>lang="en"</code>)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Known limitations</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Third-party game embeds are outside our control. Once a game loads in its sandboxed frame, accessibility
        depends on the game publisher.
      </li>
      <li>
        Some game thumbnails are provided by third parties and may have limited descriptive text beyond the game title.
      </li>
      <li>
        Advertising frames (when enabled) are provided by Google or other networks and may have their own accessibility characteristics.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Compatibility</h2>
    <p>
      The Site is designed to work with current evergreen browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge) and common
      assistive technologies. Older browsers may receive a degraded experience.
    </p>

    <h2>Ongoing improvements</h2>
    <p>
      We continue to prioritize fixes that improve core browsing and reading experiences on our first-party pages,
      including keyboard use, focus visibility, and assistive-technology compatibility.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
